# Lessons and platforms

- A mistake seen a second time becomes an automatic check before the next PR repeats it. Log it in `docs/lessons.md` (date, mistake, root cause, guard, where). Prefer a lint rule, then a type that rules it out, then a test, then a `vp run verify:*` check, then a written rule. A written rule must say why no check was added. The corrections ladder in `AGENTS.md` still comes first: if a code change removes the mistake, do that instead of adding a check.
- Tools and scripts run on Linux and on macOS. Do not read the Linux proc filesystem or any other Linux-only API. Daniel runs macOS. Port checks bind a socket or call `lsof`.
- No `Co-authored-by` line that contains an email in a commit message or a PR description. `vp run guards` fails on one. If the environment adds the trailer, strip it before pushing. No extra check: the guard already fails the email, and it cannot stop the hook from writing the message.
- Agents do not merge. Daniel squash-merges. That merge is the final gate.
- 2026-10-25 — Checks run once, by the author. Duplicate check runs on a fresh VM were the main cost. The reviewer reads the diff and the `## Verification` results and does not rerun `format-check`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build`, or `verify`. Guards stay in `lint`. Pre-launch there are no users yet, so mistakes are cheap. Foundations are the exception: a schema or migration, a new dependency family, or an ADR. A review Daniel asks for is separate too. Post-launch the path list in `docs/team.md` applies. The coordinator flips the phase at the first public deploy. The active phase is named in `docs/team.md`. No new check: the gate is that heading plus a path list, and a script would restate the coordinator's job. Nits do not block. Re-review only after a major, and only the changed lines. Custom modes are an account setting, so the separate-agent launch stays a written rule.
- 2026-10-25 — Each plan item is its own ticket, `.scratch/<feature-slug>/issues/<NN>-<slug>.md`, the local-markdown layout from mattpocock/skills `issue-tracker-local.md` at `5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2`. `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md` is that convention and has no item list. PRs #8 and #9 both conflicted on the shared status table after #7. Cause: every pull request edited that one file. No guard and no `plan:list` script: a check that a branch touched only its own file needs the plan id, which the diff does not name, and a table ban misses a bullet list and flags a real table. The index has no list to corrupt. Before the final push, fetch and merge `origin/main` (no rebase, no force-push) and rerun the checks when that merge changes the tree. A merge that does not change the tree leaves the recorded results in place, so the checks-run-once rule still holds.
